WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:06.170
Hi there!

2
00:00:06.171 --> 00:00:08.987
Who are

3
00:00:08.988 --> 00:00:12.857
you? I'm a

4
00:00:12.858 --> 00:00:16.525
giant anteater. Giant anteaters

5
00:00:16.526 --> 00:00:24.358
have very long tongues. Where do

6
00:00:24.359 --> 00:00:27.170
you live? Giant anteaters

7
00:00:27.171 --> 00:00:33.635
live in Central and South America. We like

8
00:00:33.636 --> 00:00:39.887
tropical forests and grasslands. Your tail

9
00:00:39.888 --> 00:00:43.697
has lots of hair! I

10
00:00:43.698 --> 00:00:47.762
use my tail as a blanket. I

11
00:00:47.763 --> 00:00:52.897
use it to block the sun too. You

12
00:00:52.898 --> 00:00:56.185
eat ants, right? Yes.

13
00:00:56.186 --> 00:01:01.693
We eat lots and lots of ants. We

14
00:01:01.694 --> 00:01:06.305
also eat termites. How

15
00:01:06.306 --> 00:01:09.741
do you find food? Giant

16
00:01:09.742 --> 00:01:17.169
anteaters have strong noses. We

17
00:01:17.170 --> 00:01:22.430
sniff for anthills and termite mounds. Then

18
00:01:22.431 --> 00:01:27.406
we dig up our food. Do

19
00:01:27.407 --> 00:01:30.743
you grab ants with your tongue? Our

20
00:01:30.744 --> 00:01:35.149
tongues are long and sticky. We

21
00:01:35.150 --> 00:01:40.732
flick our tongues into the anthill.

22
00:01:40.733 --> 00:01:45.088
Ants stick to our tongues.

23
00:01:45.089 --> 00:01:48.049
Do you have enemies?

24
00:01:48.050 --> 00:01:52.319
Pumas and jaguars hunt us.

25
00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:58.801
We fight them with our sharp claws.

26
00:01:58.802 --> 00:02:02.360
Sniff, sniff.

27
00:02:02.361 --> 00:02:04.370
I smell an anthill.

28
00:02:04.371 --> 00:02:07.294
Good-bye.

29
00:02:07.295 --> 00:02:12.368
Good-bye, Giant Anteater!

